WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:19.712
Mr. Scary, the hotel manager, greeted us when we got off the bus.

2
00:00:19.713 --> 00:00:23.968
"Mr. Scary looks scary," I whispered to Molly.

3
00:00:23.969 --> 00:00:30.064
Molly nodded. "He sure looks mysterious," she whispered back.

4
00:00:30.065 --> 00:00:36.003
"Welcome to Shadow Lake Lodge," said Mr. Scary in a deep voice.

5
00:00:36.004 --> 00:00:42.083
"You will be staying in suite 303."

6
00:00:42.084 --> 00:00:48.037
When we got to our suite, Bunch immediately started barking.

7
00:00:48.038 --> 00:00:50.959
"It's the red curtains," said Josh.

8
00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.719
"Bunch hates the color red."

9
00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:56.634
"But dogs are color-blind," I said.

10
00:00:56.635 --> 00:01:00.489
"To Bunch, everything looks gray."

11
00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:04.186
"Bunch can see colors," Josh insisted.

12
00:01:04.187 --> 00:01:09.939
"Ruff!" barked Bunch again and again at the curtains.

13
00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:14.534
"See, Iggy? Bunch doesn't like the red curtains," said Josh.

14
00:01:14.535 --> 00:01:18.049
I shrugged. Maybe Josh was right.

15
00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:21.848
Our suite didn't have gold curtains or diamond tables.

16
00:01:21.849 --> 00:01:26.957
But it was pretty cool, with a large living room and three bedrooms.

17
00:01:26.958 --> 00:01:31.882
We unpacked and then headed back downstairs.

18
00:01:31.883 --> 00:01:38.938
In the Lake Lounge room a table was loaded with fresh vegetables.

19
00:01:38.939 --> 00:01:42.791
A sign read: "Vegetable Parade for Families Today!

20
00:01:42.792 --> 00:01:47.931
Help Mr. Scary March Your Favorite Vegetables Right into The Soup Pot!"

21
00:01:47.932 --> 00:01:53.008
"Yuck!" said Caswell. "Vegetables!"

22
00:01:53.009 --> 00:01:54.691
I made a face too.

23
00:01:54.692 --> 00:02:00.338
After my last invention, I was pretty sick of vegetables myself.

24
00:02:00.339 --> 00:02:04.821
"Dad, can we hike up to the lookout tower?" asked Josh.

25
00:02:04.822 --> 00:02:07.619
"Sure," said Mr. Chen.

26
00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:10.299
"We'll go right after lunch."

27
00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:15.593
But after lunch Caswell fell sound asleep in the Lake Lounge.

28
00:02:15.594 --> 00:02:19.908
"You kids can walk up to the tower," said Mr. Chen.

29
00:02:19.909 --> 00:02:21.971
"I'll stay here with Caswell.

30
00:02:21.972 --> 00:02:29.214
But first I'd better go find a blanket for him."

31
00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:33.849
"Wait until you see my new invention," I said when we got outside.

32
00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:37.312
"What is it?" asked Jenny.

33
00:02:37.313 --> 00:02:42.503
I grinned. "It's something called rainbow trail pellets.

34
00:02:42.504 --> 00:02:46.398
I invented the pellets in case we get lost on the trail.

35
00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:49.539
After all, we're not in the city anymore.

36
00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:53.170
We're deep in the wilderness."

37
00:02:53.171 --> 00:02:56.668
I reached into my pocket and took out four bags.

38
00:02:56.669 --> 00:03:00.620
Each one was filled with brightly colored pellets.

39
00:03:00.621 --> 00:03:03.252
Josh peered at the bag.

40
00:03:03.253 --> 00:03:06.042
"Hey! Those are Sparky's hamster pellets.

41
00:03:06.043 --> 00:03:08.684
But they're all different colors."

42
00:03:08.685 --> 00:03:12.496
"I dyed them with food coloring," I said proudly.

43
00:03:12.497 --> 00:03:14.966
"That way they'll work better."

44
00:03:14.967 --> 00:03:19.595
"How does this invention work exactly?" asked Molly.

45
00:03:19.596 --> 00:03:23.318
"First you open the bag," I explained.

46
00:03:23.319 --> 00:03:25.504
"Then you put the bag in your pocket.

47
00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:29.477
The pellets will dribble out as we walk."

48
00:03:29.478 --> 00:03:31.808
"I get it," said Josh.

49
00:03:31.809 --> 00:03:36.917
"If we take the wrong trail and get stranded, people can just follow the pellets!"

50
00:03:36.918 --> 00:03:39.700
"Right!" I said.

51
00:03:39.701 --> 00:03:49.241
The four of us started up one of the trails to the lookout tower.

52
00:03:49.242 --> 00:03:53.908
When we reached the top, we were amazed by the view.

53
00:03:53.909 --> 00:03:58.294
"You can see for miles up here!" said Jenny.

54
00:03:58.295 --> 00:04:03.069
"Hey." Josh reached around to check his back pocket.

55
00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:05.802
"My bag of pellets is empty."

56
00:04:05.803 --> 00:04:09.766
"Mine is too," said Molly and Jenny.

57
00:04:09.767 --> 00:04:11.315
I felt in my pocket.

58
00:04:11.316 --> 00:04:14.223
My bag was also empty.

59
00:04:14.224 --> 00:04:17.969
"The pellets worked perfectly!" I declared.

60
00:04:17.970 --> 00:04:21.957
"If we were stranded, people would be able to find us."

61
00:04:21.958 --> 00:04:26.872
"It's another one of Iggy's brilliant inventions!" said Josh.

62
00:04:26.873 --> 00:04:32.570
"I'm glad we're not really stranded though," said Jenny.

63
00:04:32.571 --> 00:04:39.864
We explored the lookout tower for a while and then headed back to the hotel.

64
00:04:39.865 --> 00:04:45.466
When we arrived back at the Lake Lounge room, Caswell was wide-awake.

65
00:04:45.467 --> 00:04:48.444
He was playing checkers with Mr. Chen.

66
00:04:48.445 --> 00:04:54.552
Nearby Mr. Scary, the hotel manager, was wringing his hands.

67
00:04:54.553 --> 00:04:59.059
"A disaster has happened!" he cried.

68
00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:01.410
"All my vegetables have disappeared!

69
00:05:01.411 --> 00:05:04.670
My vegetable parade is ruined!"

70
00:05:04.671 --> 00:05:07.033
Mr. Scary was right.

71
00:05:07.034 --> 00:05:11.274
The vegetables for the parade had vanished.

72
00:05:11.275 --> 00:05:16.780
"I will find the thief who stole my vegetables," cried Mr. Scary.

73
00:05:16.781 --> 00:05:22.484
"And I will punish him!"
